WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 2.1 · Theory of Change
Understanding Theory of Change

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A Theory of Change lets you test your idea on paper before you launch.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.133
A Theory of Change makes your reasoning explicit: if we do this work, why might a particular change follow? It sets out the steps from your work to the change, and the assumptions that connect them.

4
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:29.133
Three spheres, one pathway

5
00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:41.574
Control: Inputs, activities and outputs: what you put in, what you do and what you deliver. For example: Two founders’ time and a borrowed hall; 12 repair cafés in the first year.

6
00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:50.681
Influence: Outcomes: changes in the people and institutions you work with directly. For example: Residents learn simple repairs and repair before buying new.

7
00:00:50.681 --> 00:01:01.730
Contribute: Impact: wider change that many actors shape, so your claims get more modest. For example: Less waste and lower household costs in the town.

8
00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:02.730
Why it matters

9
00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:08.033
1. You test your idea on paper before you spend money.

10
00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:14.078
2. It shows partners and funders why your work should lead to change.

11
00:01:14.078 --> 00:01:20.011
3. Modest claims build trust while your idea is untested.

12
00:01:20.411 --> 00:01:21.011
How you will use it

13
00:01:21.011 --> 00:01:25.204
1. One pathway for each external strategic objective.

14
00:01:25.204 --> 00:01:29.396
2. Internal objectives appear as inputs and conditions.

15
00:01:29.396 --> 00:01:34.959
3. Your indicators and reviews, later in the course.

16
00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:35.959
What to avoid

17
00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:41.263
A diagram of arrows with no explanation of each link.

18
00:01:41.263 --> 00:01:45.456
Claiming the wider impact as yours alone.

19
00:01:45.456 --> 00:01:52.130
Treating it as fixed instead of revising it when evidence disagrees.

20
00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:54.530
You write the change argument for your first external objective.

21
00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:58.530
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:03.130
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
